
========================================================================
CHECK 1  braid defining polynomial and REAL chamber count
========================================================================
  n=2: (-1)^(n-1)*chi(-1)=2; n!=2; equal? True
  n=3: (-1)^(n-1)*chi(-1)=6; n!=6; equal? True
  n=4: (-1)^(n-1)*chi(-1)=24; n!=24; equal? True
  n=5: (-1)^(n-1)*chi(-1)=120; n!=120; equal? True
  n=6: (-1)^(n-1)*chi(-1)=720; n!=720; equal? True
  n=7: (-1)^(n-1)*chi(-1)=5040; n!=5040; equal? True
  V(a)=prod_(i<j)(a_j-a_i) vanishes exactly on braid hyperplanes.
  Scope: n! counts chambers of the REAL complement; the complex complement is connected.

========================================================================
CHECK 2  leading coalescence; vanishing order is NOT codimension
========================================================================
  epsilon=0.1: V/leading=0.979408049
  epsilon=0.01: V/leading=0.997994008
  epsilon=0.001: V/leading=0.999799940
  block sizes 3+2: vanishing order=4, codimension=3
  The cross-block factor is a nonzero unit near this generic flat.

========================================================================
CHECK 3  explicit companion determinant and full-rank gap diagonal
========================================================================
  g=1: det coeffs=[1, -1, -1]; expected=[1, -1, -1]; det PASS? True; diagonal PASS? True
  g=2: det coeffs=[1, -1, 0, -1]; expected=[1, -1, 0, -1]; det PASS? True; diagonal PASS? True
  g=3: det coeffs=[1, -1, 0, 0, -1]; expected=[1, -1, 0, 0, -1]; det PASS? True; diagonal PASS? True
  g=4: det coeffs=[1, -1, 0, 0, 0, -1]; expected=[1, -1, 0, 0, 0, -1]; det PASS? True; diagonal PASS? True
  g=5: det coeffs=[1, -1, 0, 0, 0, 0, -1]; expected=[1, -1, 0, 0, 0, 0, -1]; det PASS? True; diagonal PASS? True
  The companion digraph has a loop; it is not a tournament adjacency matrix.

========================================================================
NON-RESULTS MADE EXPLICIT
========================================================================
  - No general NC2 iff follows from the special THM-2033 Vandermonde matrix.
  - No hyper-Bessel block product follows from the coalescence formula.
  - THM-2023 proves Phi_(p,q) Laguerre--Polya independently.
  - No bagel-cut Euler complex or bagel/shadow valuation is computed here.
  - bagel(n)=cake(n+1)-2 remains the strongest direct cutting identity.
